  "strategy": "3. ...\n    d. For each point in the neighborhood around the best solution found at the current resolution, generate new candidate solutions by small perturbations. Use a small step size (like 0.01) and allow negative updates (decrease) to the function value.\n    e. Maintain two dictionaries, `best_at_res` and `best_global`, to keep track of the best solution found at each resolution and the globally best solution.\n    f. After the optimization at each resolution, update the candidate pool with the new solution.\n    g. Schedule the next resolution n_next by examining the improvement rate and doubling the increments if needed.\n\n4. ...\n    a. Identify several meaningful variations: different initializations, different step sizes (0.01, 0.02, 0.05, 0.1), different neighborhood exploration radii (5%, 10%, 20%, 50% of the grid), and different optimization circularness penalty terms (0, 1e-3, 1e-5, 1e-7).\n    b. ...\n\n5. ...\n    d. Estimation: Each resolution requires O(10 seconds)\n    e. Check deadlines on a separate thread for each resolution optimization.\n    f. ...\n    g. Implementation:\n\n        def run_optimization(seed, initial_h, n, deadline):\n            best_c = None\n            best_h = None\n            # ... (parameters and optimization code)\n\n        def run(seed=42, budget_s=1100, **kwargs):\n            t0 = time.time()\n            deadline = t0 + budget_s\n            rng = np.random.RandomState(seed)\n            best_global = None\n            current_res = 500\n            best_at_res = {500: None}\n            ...\n            # Optimization loop over resolutions\n            ...\n            while improve_required and time_left and next_res <= 1000:\n                # Prepare and run the optimization for next_res\n                ...\n                best_h, best_c, n_pt = run_optimization(seed, initial_h, next_res, deadline)\n                ...\n\n            return best_h, best_c, next_res or initial_res\n\n6. ...\n\nAfter validation, return only the candidate h_values that improve the best_global. Ensure the final h_values satisfy the integral constraint by re-projecting after final selection. Validate the objective value by recomputing with the exact numerical integration.",
